  "notes": "VERB TYPE:\n{他動詞|たどうし} (transitive verb)\n\nGodan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}) ending in る\n・{怖|こわ}がらない (negative)\n・{怖|こわ}がって (te-form)\n・{怖|こわ}がった (past)\n\nGRAMMAR NOTE:\nThis is the -がる form of the i-adjective {怖|こわ}い. The -がる suffix converts adjectives describing internal feelings into verbs that describe observable behavior.\n\n{怖|こわ}い vs {怖|こわ}がる:\n・{怖|こわ}い - (I am) scared, frightening\n・{怖|こわ}がる - to be afraid of, to show fear (observed behavior)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・〜を{怖|こわ}がる - to be afraid of ~\n・{怖|こわ}がらせる - to frighten, to scare (causative)\n・{怖|こわ}がり - a scaredy-cat, timid person (noun form)\n\nRELATED -がる VERBS:\n・{欲|ほ}しがる - to want (from {欲|ほ}しい)\n・{恥|は}ずかしがる - to be shy (from {恥|は}ずかしい)\n・{寂|さび}しがる - to feel lonely (from {寂|さび}しい)",
